{
  "response": "Thanks — I can help. Quick summary of how savings interest works (from our policy) and what might explain the amount you saw, plus next steps if you want me to check your account.",
  "how_interest_is_calculated": "Savings interest accrues daily using a daily periodic rate derived from your APY and is credited monthly. Your applicable APY can include: the account base APY, a single checking-account \"linked\" APY boost (only the highest checking boost applies), a single credit-card APY bonus (only the highest card bonus applies), and any small relationship bonus for holding products together. If your balance moves between tiers during the month, interest is calculated each day on that day's balance.",
  "common_reasons_the_amount_might_look_low": [
    "The APY applied to your account may be the base Gold APY (or base + small relationship bonus) — not all boosts apply.",
    "Only the highest checking-account boost and only the highest credit-card bonus are applied (they do not stack with others of the same type).",
    "Your average daily balance during the cycle may have been lower than the snapshot balance you quoted, which reduces the monthly credit.",
    "Month length and daily compounding mean the posted monthly dollar amount can vary even at the same APY."
  ],
  "quick_math_examples_for_a_96_000_balance": {
    "If_APY_is_5.5_percent_(base_Gold)": {
      "monthly_interest_estimate": 440,
      "calculation_note": "96,000 * 0.055 / 12 = 440"
    },
    "If_APY_is_5.525_percent_(5.5_plus_0.025_relationship_bonus)": {
      "monthly_interest_estimate": 441
    },
    "If_APY_is_6.1_percent_(5.5_plus_a_0.6_card_bonus_example)": {
      "monthly_interest_estimate": 488
    },
    "Implied_annual_rate_from_450_monthly_payment": {
      "implied_apy": 5.625,
      "note": "450 * 12 / 96,000 = 0.05625 (≈5.625% annualized), which is close to the base Gold rate."
    },
    "conclusion": "So $450 on a $96k balance is roughly in line with the documented Gold base APY — not necessarily evidence of an error."
  },
  "offer_to_investigate": "If you want me to review your specific accounts and confirm you're receiving all eligible boosts/bonuses (and to correct anything if it’s wrong), I can do that. To access your account details I need to verify your identity first.",
  "verification_requirements": "Per our process I need to confirm any TWO of the following: date of birth, email address, phone number, or mailing address. Once you provide two and I verify them, I will: 1) look up all your Rho-Bank accounts, 2) check which checking account boost and which credit-card bonus (if any) was applied, 3) review the interest posting for the statement period, 4) calculate expected vs actual interest, and 5) if there’s a discrepancy I can apply an interest correction credit and submit an investigation report.",
  "next_action_for_you": "Tell me whether you'd like me to proceed with an account review. If yes, please tell me which TWO of (date of birth, email, phone number, mailing address) you prefer to confirm now.",
  "note_on_privacy_and_limits": "I will only access your accounts after you verify. If after review the issue requires backend investigation I will apply a corrective credit first (if applicable) and then file an interest discrepancy report on your behalf."
}

